[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary: Kynetic Spec - Key File Patterns & Architecture\n\nBased on my analysis of the codebase, here are the detailed patterns and structures:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **INBOX COMMANDS** (`src/cli/commands/inbox.ts`)\n\n#### Command Registration Pattern\n```typescript\nexport function registerInboxCommands(program: Command): void {\n  const inbox = program.command(\"inbox\")\n    .description(\"Low-friction capture for ideas\");\n  \n  markMutating(inbox.command(\"add <text>\"))\n    .option(\"--tag <tag...>\", \"Add tags\")\n    .action(async (text: string, options) => { ... });\n}\n```\n\n#### Key Commands & Patterns\n\n**1. `inbox add <text>`**\n- Creates inbox item via `createInboxItem(input, configAuthor)`\n- Saves via `saveInboxItem(ctx, item)`\n- Commits with: `commitIfShadow(ctx.shadow, \"inbox-add\", undefined, text)`\n- JSON output: `success(message, { item })`\n- Error handling: `error(errors.failures.addInboxItem, err); process.exit(EXIT_CODES.ERROR)`\n\n**2. `inbox promote <ref>` → Creates task from inbox item**\n- Resolves ref: `resolveInboxRef(ref, items)` → `findInboxItemByRef(items, ref)` \n- Validates priority: `parseIntOption(options.priority, { min: 1, max: 5 })`\n- Validates spec_ref: `validateSpecRef(specRef, refIndex, allTasks, allItems)`\n- Interactive title prompt if not provided: `await prompt(\"Task title: \")`\n- Creates task: `createTask(taskInput)` with optional note via `createNote()`\n- Optional: Deletes inbox item unless `--keep` flag\n- Commits: `commitIfShadow(ctx.shadow, \"inbox-promote\", taskRef)`\n- JSON output: `success(message, { task })`\n\n**3. `inbox delete <ref>`**\n- Confirmation prompt: `await prompt(\"Are you sure? (y/N): \")`\n- Deletes via: `deleteInboxItem(ctx, item._ulid)`\n- Commits: `commitIfShadow(ctx.shadow, \"inbox-delete\", itemUlidSlice)`\n- JSON output: `success(message)`\n\n**4. `inbox list`**\n- Loads: `loadInboxItems(ctx)`\n- Filters by tag if provided\n- Sorts oldest-first by default (or `--newest` for reverse)\n- Supports `--count` for item count\n- Supports `--limit <n>`\n- JSON output: array of items\n\n**5. `inbox get <ref>`**\n- Resolves and displays full item details\n- JSON output: single item object\n\n**6. `inbox set <ref>`**\n- Updates content: `--content <text>`\n- Manages tags: `--tag <tag...>`, `--clear-tags`\n- Tracks updates in array and commits with joined summary\n- Commits: `commitIfShadow(ctx.shadow, \"inbox-set\", ref, \"content, tags\")`\n\n**7. `inbox note <ref> <text>`**\n- Appends note with separator: `\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n\"`\n- Commits: `commitIfShadow(ctx.shadow, \"inbox-note\", ref)`\n\n#### Error Handling Patterns\n```typescript\ntry {\n  // operation\n  success(message, { item }); // JSON output\n} catch (err) {\n  error(errors.failures.addInboxItem, err);\n  process.exit(EXIT_CODES.ERROR);\n}\n```\n\n#### Output Patterns\n- Terminal: `console.log()` + `success()` helper\n- JSON mode: `output(data, terminalCallback)` wraps both formats\n- Exit codes: `EXIT_CODES.ERROR`, `EXIT_CODES.NOT_FOUND`, `EXIT_CODES.VALIDATION_FAILED`\n\n---\n\n### 2. **TRIAGE SCHEMA** (`src/schema/triage.ts`)\n\n#### Type Definitions (Zod schemas)\n\n**TriageStatusSchema** - Lifecycle states\n```typescript\nexport const TriageStatusSchema = z.enum([\"pending\", \"triaged\", \"acted_on\"]);\n```\n\n**TriageActionSchema** - Decision types\n```typescript\nexport const TriageActionSchema = z.enum([\n  \"promote\",      // Convert to task\n  \"delete\",       // Remove inbox item\n  \"defer\",        // Postpone decision\n  \"spec-gap\",     // Need spec clarification\n  \"duplicate\",    // Duplicate of another item\n]);\n```\n\n**TriageRecordSchema** - Full triage record with validation\n```typescript\nexport const TriageRecordSchema = z.object({\n  _ulid: UlidSchema,\n  inbox_ref: UlidSchema,                    // Source inbox item\n  item_snapshot: z.string().min(1),         // Snapshot of inbox text at triage time\n  status: TriageStatusSchema,\n  \n  // Decision fields (required if status=\"triaged\")\n  action: TriageActionSchema.optional(),\n  reasoning: z.string().optional(),\n  decided_by: z.string().optional(),\n  evidence_refs: z.array(RefSchema).default([]),\n  \n  // Override fields\n  override_reasoning: z.string().optional(),\n  override_by: z.string().optional(),\n  override_at: DateTimeSchema.optional(),\n  \n  // Execution fields\n  acted_at: DateTimeSchema.optional(),       // Set when acted_on status reached\n  result_ref: RefSchema.optional(),          // Ref to created task/etc\n  \n  created_at: DateTimeSchema,\n  updated_at: DateTimeSchema.optional(),\n}).superRefine((data, ctx) => {\n  // AC-3: Enforce decision metadata for \"triaged\" status\n  if (data.status === \"triaged\") {\n    if (!data.action) ctx.addIssue({ ... }); // \"triaged records require an action\"\n    if (!data.reasoning) ctx.addIssue({ ... }); // \"triaged records require reasoning\"\n    if (!data.decided_by) ctx.addIssue({ ... }); // \"triaged records require decided_by\"\n  }\n  \n  // AC-5: Enforce acted_at + decision metadata for \"acted_on\" status\n  if (data.status === \"acted_on\") {\n    if (!data.acted_at) ctx.addIssue({ ... }); // \"acted-on records require acted_at\"\n    // Also enforce AC-3 decision metadata inheritance\n    if (!data.action) ctx.addIssue({ ... });\n    if (!data.reasoning) ctx.addIssue({ ... });\n    if (!data.decided_by) ctx.addIssue({ ... });\n  }\n});\n```\n\n**TriageFileSchema** - File format wrapper\n```typescript\nexport const TriageFileSchema = z.object({\n  kynetic_triage: z.string().default(\"1.0\"),\n  triage: z.array(TriageRecordSchema),\n});\n```\n\n#### Exported Types\n```typescript\nexport type TriageStatus = \"pending\" | \"triaged\" | \"acted_on\";\nexport type TriageAction = \"promote\" | \"delete\" | \"defer\" | \"spec-gap\" | \"duplicate\";\nexport type TriageRecord = { /* full record */ };\nexport type TriageRecordInput = { /* input subset without _sourceFile */ };\nexport type TriageFile = { kynetic_triage: string; triage: TriageRecord[] };\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. **TRIAGE PARSER FUNCTIONS** (`src/parser/yaml.ts`, lines 1850-2025)\n\n#### Path & Loading\n```typescript\nexport function getTriageFilePath(ctx: KspecContext): string {\n  return path.join(ctx.specDir, \"project.triage.yaml\");\n  // Returns: .kspec/project.triage.yaml (shadow) or spec/project.triage.yaml (traditional)\n}\n\nexport async function loadTriageRecords(ctx: KspecContext): Promise<LoadedTriageRecord[]> {\n  // Loads triage file (handles both { triage: [...] } and raw array formats)\n  // Returns array with _sourceFile metadata attached\n  // Returns [] if file doesn't exist or parse fails\n}\n```\n\n#### Record Type Definition\n```typescript\nexport interface LoadedTriageRecord extends TriageRecord {\n  _sourceFile?: string; // Runtime metadata for write-back\n}\n```\n\n#### CRUD Operations\n\n**Save (upsert on inbox_ref uniqueness)**\n```typescript\nexport async function saveTriageRecord(\n  ctx: KspecContext,\n  record: LoadedTriageRecord,\n): Promise<void> {\n  // AC-8: One record per inbox_ref (upserts by ULID first, then inbox_ref)\n  // AC-9: Sets updated_at = new Date().toISOString() on every mutation\n  // Saves to { kynetic_triage: \"1.0\", triage: [...] } format\n}\n```\n\n**Find by ULID or short ULID**\n```typescript\nexport function findTriageRecordByRef(\n  records: LoadedTriageRecord[],\n  ref: string,\n): LoadedTriageRecord | undefined {\n  // Strips @ prefix if present\n  // Matches full ULID or short ULID prefix\n  // Returns first match or undefined\n}\n```\n\n**Find by inbox item reference (for upsert)**\n```typescript\nexport function findTriageRecordByInboxRef(\n  records: LoadedTriageRecord[],\n  inboxRef: string,\n): LoadedTriageRecord | undefined {\n  // Finds record where inbox_ref === cleanRef\n  // Used for one-record-per-inbox-item enforcement\n}\n```\n\n#### File Format Examples\n```yaml\nkynetic_triage: \"1.0\"\ntriage:\n  - _ulid: 01JHNKAB0G0R40WXX4F3Z7MQ3A\n    inbox_ref: 01JHNKAB0G0R40WXX4F3Z7M001\n    item_snapshot: \"Original inbox text at triage time\"\n    status: pending\n    created_at: \"2026-02-22T03:46:16.946Z\"\n    \n  - _ulid: 01JHNKAB0G0R40WXX4F3Z7MQ3B\n    inbox_ref: 01JHNKAB0G0R40WXX4F3Z7M002\n    item_snapshot: \"Another inbox item\"\n    status: triaged\n    action: promote\n    reasoning: \"Clear feature request, should become task\"\n    decided_by: \"@claude\"\n    evidence_refs: [\"@spec-item\"]\n    created_at: \"2026-02-22T03:46:16.946Z\"\n    updated_at: \"2026-02-22T04:00:00.000Z\"\n    \n  - _ulid: 01JHNKAB0G0R40WXX4F3Z7MQ3C\n    inbox_ref: 01JHNKAB0G0R40WXX4F3Z7M003\n    item_snapshot: \"Item being acted on\"\n    status: acted_on\n    action: spec-gap\n    reasoning: \"Needs spec review before implementation\"\n    decided_by: \"@claude\"\n    acted_at: \"2026-02-22T04:15:30.000Z\"\n    result_ref: \"@observation-001\"\n    created_at: \"2026-02-22T03:46:16.946Z\"\n    updated_at: \"2026-02-22T04:15:30.000Z\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. **OBSERVATIONS (for spec-gap action)** (`src/parser/meta.ts`, lines 478-550)\n\n#### Creation Pattern\n```typescript\nexport function createObservation(\n  type: ObservationType,  // \"friction\" | \"success\" | \"question\" | \"idea\"\n  content: string,\n  options: {\n    workflow_ref?: string;     // Optional workflow reference\n    author?: string;           // Explicit author\n    configAuthor?: string | null;  // Config author for fallback\n  } = {},\n): Observation {\n  return {\n    _ulid: ulid(),\n    type,\n    content,\n    workflow_ref: options.workflow_ref,\n    created_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n    author: options.author ?? getAuthor(options.configAuthor),\n    resolved: false,\n    resolution: null,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n#### Saving\n```typescript\nexport async function saveObservation(\n  ctx: KspecContext,\n  observation: LoadedObservation,\n): Promise<void> {\n  // Loads existing meta manifest or creates new\n  // Upserts by _ulid\n  // Saves to manifest path (derived from manifest name)\n}\n```\n\n#### Meta Observe Command Integration\n(`src/cli/commands/meta.ts`, lines 715-850)\n\n**Standard flow:**\n```typescript\nmarkMutating(meta.command(\"observe [type] [content]\"))\n  .option(\"--workflow <ref>\", \"Reference to workflow\")\n  .option(\"--author <author>\", \"Author of observation\")\n  .option(\"--from-inbox <ref>\", \"Convert inbox item to observation\")\n  .option(\"--type <type>\", \"Override type when using --from-inbox\")\n  .action(async (type, content, options) => {\n    const ctx = await initContext();\n    \n    // Case 1: Convert from inbox item\n    if (options.fromInbox) {\n      const inboxItems = await loadInboxItems(ctx);\n      const item = findInboxItemByRef(inboxItems, options.fromInbox);\n      const observationType = (options.type || \"idea\") as ObservationType;\n      \n      const observation = createObservation(\n        observationType,\n        item.text,  // Use inbox item text as content\n        {\n          workflow_ref: options.workflow,\n          author: options.author,\n          configAuthor: ctx.config?.identity?.author,\n        },\n      );\n      \n      await saveObservation(ctx, observation);\n      await deleteInboxItem(ctx, item._ulid);\n      await commitIfShadow(\n        ctx.shadow,\n        \"meta-observe-from-inbox\",\n        observation._ulid.substring(0, 8),\n        `Convert inbox item to ${observationType} observation`,\n      );\n      \n      output(observation, () =>\n        success(`Created observation: ${shortUlid}`),\n      );\n    }\n    // Case 2: Direct observation creation\n    else {\n      const observation = createObservation(type, content, { ... });\n      await saveObservation(ctx, observation);\n      await commitIfShadow(ctx.shadow, \"meta-observe\", shortUlid, type);\n      output(observation, () => success(`Created observation: ${shortUlid}`));\n    }\n  });\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. **CLI COMMAND REGISTRATION** (`src/cli/index.ts`)\n\n#### Pattern\n```typescript\nimport { Command } from \"commander\";\n\nconst program = new Command();\n\nprogram\n  .name(\"kspec\")\n  .version(version)\n  .option(\"--json\", \"Output in JSON format\")\n  .option(\"--yaml\", \"Output in YAML format\")\n  .hook(\"preAction\", async (thisCommand, actionCommand) => {\n    // Set output mode, auto-start daemon, etc.\n  });\n\n// Register command groups (order matters - traits added to item subcommands)\nregisterTasksCommands(program);\nregisterTaskCommands(program);\nregisterInboxCommands(program);\nregisterMetaCommands(program);\n// ... more registrations\n\n// Error handling for unknown commands\nprogram.on(\"command:*\", (operands) => {\n  // Suggest closest match\n});\n\nexport { program };\n```\n\n#### Shadow Commit Pattern (used by all mutating commands)\n```typescript\nawait commitIfShadow(\n  ctx.shadow,           // ShadowConfig | null\n  \"inbox-promote\",      // operation name (used in commit message)\n  taskSlug,             // ref (optional - item identifier)\n  \"detail\",             // detail (optional - extra context)\n);\n```\n\n**commitIfShadow signature:**\n```typescript\nexport async function commitIfShadow(\n  shadowConfig: ShadowConfig | null,\n  operation: string,\n  ref?: string,\n  detail?: string,\n  verbose?: boolean,\n): Promise<boolean>;\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. **KEY PATTERNS & CONVENTIONS**\n\n#### Error Handling\n- All commands catch errors → `error(errors.failures.X, err)` → `process.exit(EXIT_CODES.ERROR)`\n- Validation errors: `EXIT_CODES.VALIDATION_FAILED`\n- Not found errors: `EXIT_CODES.NOT_FOUND`\n- Usage errors: `EXIT_CODES.USAGE_ERROR`\n\n#### JSON Output\n```typescript\n// Pattern 1: Item + terminal display\noutput(item, () => {\n  console.log(`Display text for terminal`);\n});\n\n// Pattern 2: Success message with metadata\nsuccess(`Message`, { item });\n\n// Pattern 3: Just output\noutput(items, () => { /* terminal version */ });\n```\n\n#### Context Initialization\n```typescript\nconst ctx = await initContext();\n// Provides:\n// - rootDir: project root\n// - specDir: .kspec/ (shadow) or spec/ (traditional)\n// - manifestPath: path to manifest\n// - manifest: parsed manifest (or null)\n// - shadow: ShadowConfig | null\n// - config: ResolvedKspecConfig\n```\n\n#### Author Resolution Chain (in order)\n1. `KSPEC_AUTHOR` env var (explicit agent config)\n2. `ctx.config?.identity?.author` (kspec.config.yaml)\n3. `git config user.name` (git identity)\n4. `USER`/`USERNAME` env var (system user)\n5. `undefined` (no author detected)\n\n#### Reference Resolution\n- Supports `@` prefix (`@task-slug` or `@01JHNK...`)\n- Looks for full ULID match first\n- Falls back to short ULID prefix match (case-insensitive)\n- Then checks slug matches\n\n#### markMutating Annotation\n```typescript\nmarkMutating(inbox.command(\"add <text>\"))\n  // Marks command as mutating (modifies spec/task state)\n  // Used for command-level annotations\n```\n\n#### Tag Parsing\n```typescript\nparseTagsArray(options.tag)  // Converts CLI --tag to string array\n// Handles: --tag a b c → [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. **SUMMARY TABLE: Key Functions & Their Purposes**\n\n| File | Function | Purpose |\n|------|----------|---------|\n| `inbox.ts` | `registerInboxCommands(program)` | Register all inbox subcommands |\n| `inbox.ts` | `resolveInboxRef(ref, items)` | Find inbox item, exit if not found |\n| `yaml.ts` | `loadTriageRecords(ctx)` | Load all triage records from project |\n| `yaml.ts` | `saveTriageRecord(ctx, record)` | Upsert triage record (by inbox_ref) |\n| `yaml.ts` | `findTriageRecordByRef(records, ref)` | Find triage by ULID |\n| `yaml.ts` | `findTriageRecordByInboxRef(records, ref)` | Find triage by inbox item ref |\n| `yaml.ts` | `getTriageFilePath(ctx)` | Get .kspec/project.triage.yaml path |\n| `meta.ts` | `createObservation(type, content, options)` | Create observation object |\n| `meta.ts` | `saveObservation(ctx, observation)` | Save to meta manifest |\n| `shadow.ts` | `commitIfShadow(config, op, ref, detail)` | Auto-commit to kspec-meta branch |\n| `index.ts` | `registerXCommands(program)` | Register command group (called in order) |\n\n---\n\nThis summary covers the complete architecture for inbox management, triage records, observations, and CLI command registration patterns used throughout the kynetic-spec project."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab61a3f (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 73536\ntool_uses: 24\nduration_ms: 68829</usage>"}]